{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779327803,"nonce":"FoInCFF2Opg1IDJYMnX6if54X+o=","title":"Studio: make Task sidebar resizable with local timeline overflow","message":"## Problem\n\nThe Model projection's component sidebar can be resized, but the Task projection's task sidebar is fixed width. For delayed-reach task setup, the epoch-structure table is too narrow by default and its column headers can be squeezed until they become unreadable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Make the Task projection sidebar user-resizable.\n- Use a wider default width, roughly one third of the available page/canvas region.\n- Keep task-data port interactions working: dragging from task-data port symbols must start a binding edge, not a sidebar resize.\n- Prevent narrow sidebars from crushing timeline/epoch tables; elements that need width should get local horizontal overflow rather than making the whole task configuration pane scroll horizontally.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Task sidebar width can be adjusted by dragging the sidebar/canvas boundary.\n- Default Task sidebar width is materially wider than the Model component palette.\n- Delayed-reach epoch/timeline controls keep readable minimum column widths and scroll locally when needed.\n- Task-data port drag/create/select behavior is not intercepted by the resize handle.\n\nRelated: bd5aefb.","files":null}]}